okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: '그럼 ciel runtime 라우터가 한번에 여러개의 세션을 서빙하는데 문제가 없을까?' - is the router safe when several CLI sessions are served at once? Code review only; no live two-session load test was run (the launch policy would terminate the live session this work runs in)."
answer: "The transport layer is built for N clients and holds no session state, and the stateful repositories lock or write atomically. What is NOT per-session is everything the router reads from the instance: the provider/model selection, the rate-limit and cooldown budget, the single-slot activity files, and the management layer (channel/wake/restart/input) that assumes one active session. So 'no problem' cannot be asserted for independent sessions; without per-session keying the sessions interfere."
concurrency_safe:
  transport: "ciel_runtime.py:17 imports ThreadingHTTPServer; router_server_runtime.py:71-80 serves it; router_http.py has zero matches for session/thread_id/conversation/previous_response_id - each request is transformed and forwarded on its own."
  repositories: "rate_limit_repository.py wraps every read-modify-write in self.lock; runtime_activity_repository.py:119-127 writes tmp-file + replace (atomic); usage_service.py:52,58 uses an RLock and sqlite3.connect(timeout=10.0)."
  client_registry: "router_client_lifecycle.py tracks N live client pids (probe on 2026-09-21: two pids listed, dead one swept)."
shared_and_therefore_interfering:
  provider_selection: "router_http.py:1430 takes provider/pcfg from the instance config (get_current_provider(cfg)) for every LLM post; the body's model is resolved against that provider (router_http.py:1457, claude_router.py:374-377 resolve_requested_model), and a claude-* alias falls back to the provider's current_model (provider_model_selection.py:326-329). So two CLI sessions cannot use different providers, and a Claude session's model collapses to the instance's current_model. The one per-request override path is the remote bridge (x-ciel-runtime-provider/-model/-api-key), gated by bridge.enabled(cfg) and its token (router_http.py:1432-1456)."
  rate_limit_and_cooldown: "apply_router_rate_limit(provider, pcfg, upstream_model) (claude_router.py:395) draws from per-key timestamps in rate-limit-state.json, and a 429 puts the key on a cooldown for the whole instance (api_key_cooldown.py, rate_limit_repository.py:112-128); two sessions share the RPM budget and each other's cooldowns/key rotation."
  single_slot_files: "router-activity.json, context-compact-activity.json, context-usage.json (runtime_activity_repository.py:37-115 write one record each), router-last-sse.json, runtime-interaction.json, channel-compact-request.json, tool-calls.jsonl - last-writer-wins, so status surfaces flap between sessions."
  management_layer: "channel/wake transcript scope (one dict, ciel_runtime.py:4471), restart slot (one file, one target pid), submit_input ('the active session'), session socket target (one) - all already listed in multi-session-cloning.okf."
  usage_attribution: "UsageEvent has a session_id field (usage_events.py:16) but the router's response path never fills it (request_trace.py:58-64 constructs provider/model/tokens only); session_id is only echoed back when reading the ledger (usage_service.py:444). Per-session usage is therefore not attributable from the router path today."
  launch_policy: "A new launch terminates the instance's active clients and takes the port (router_process_lifecycle.py:151-211; runtime_launch.py:976-984 for Codex), so two concurrent sessions are prevented before the router ever sees them."
inferred_not_measured:
  - "JSONL dumps (requests.jsonl, responses.jsonl, router-sse-trace.jsonl, tool-calls.jsonl) are appended without a lock (request_trace.py:321-323, sse_trace.py:172-173); O_APPEND makes a single write() atomic, but a large record can be split across writes and interleave. Not measured."
  - "Two heavy streams share the GIL; router_client_lifecycle.py:248-251 already notes health probes timing out while 'its Python worker holds the GIL projecting a very large prompt'. Expected latency coupling, not corruption. Not measured."
  - "No corruption of the single-slot JSON files is expected because of the tmp+replace writes, but this was not tested under concurrency."
not_done:
  - "No live two-session load test (it would terminate this session's own router client by policy)."
  - "No push of this entry yet."
